diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 99a84fa..29462f5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ This fork adds what [Grok Bot Office](https://github.com/swissmarley/grok-bot-of
 - `grokbot bots --json` also gives each Bot's `avatar` (`shape`, `color`, `hasPhoto`), whether it is the `main` Bot, and the Bot computer's `computerPhase`. If the adapter can't read them, the plain list still works.
 - `grokbot open <bot>` shows that Bot's conversation and brings Grok Bot to the front, like clicking it in the sidebar. Focusing the window wakes the Bot's computer, so use it only when the user asks.
 - `grokbot office-watch` streams, as JSON lines, the tool each Bot is using (`browser`, `shell`, `file`, `editor`, or `null` while thinking or idle). Bots that write their own status line ("cercando sul web") expose only that text, passed on as `status`. `bots --json` carries the same `tool`, `toolName` and `status`. It also says when a Bot's question with options is waiting for your answer (`{"type":"question","open":true}`), which the app itself doesn't count as waiting on you.
+- `grokbot cards <bot>` lists the cards waiting on you (Auto Review approvals, email drafts, and ones only the app can answer); `grokbot resolve <bot> <entry> allow_once|deny|discard` answers one through the same action as its button. It re-reads the card first and refuses anything the card doesn't offer; it never uses "always allow" and never sends a draft. `office-watch` also streams `{"type":"cards"}` when a Bot's cards change.
 - `grokbot internals` reports which of these pieces the current app version still exposes (`--json` for scripts).
 
 `bun test` runs the adapter against a fake renderer shaped like Grok Bot 0.78.1.
